    "doc": {
      "text_zh": "圣器档案 SA-0441 · 版级：定版 / Fixum\n\n物品描述：一截铁制导尺，约三十二指宽，边缘因长期摩擦而磨薄，刻有均匀间隔的凹槽。铸字坊第一层回收，原归属不明。\n\n发现经过：M.2██.04，D-3847 于第 I 层铸字坊工位作业期间主动上交，称",
      "text_en": "Sacred Artifact Log SA-0441 · Gradus Formae: Fixum\n\nDescription: An iron composing rule, approximately thirty-two finger-widths in length. Edges worn thin by repeated handling. Uniform notches carved at regular intervals. Recovered from Layer I casting floor. Prior ownership: unestablished.\n\nRecovery: M.2██.04. D-3847 voluntarily relinquished the item mid-shift, stating it \"kept measuring things she wasn't measuring.\" D-3847 was reassigned per §4.2. No further incidents attributed to that personnel number.\n\nObservation: Keystruck lead slugs handled near SA-0441 during inscription have been documented as producing hairline fractures inconsistent with standard wear. Observed in ██ of ██ recorded shifts. Cause unestablished.\n\nNote: D-4012 requested the item be issued to her work station. Request granted. D-4012 reported no anomalies. Fracture incidents ceased.\n\nThe rule has not been measured since M.2██.09. The last recorded length was 31 finger-widths. Prior record: 32.\n\n[No discrepancy flag filed. No further action required.]"
    }
