    "doc": {
      "text_zh": "【回收物 RC-2291 · 发现于第 V 层排字区 D-████ 工位 · 纸质便条，装于键座横缝内】\n\n字从缝里钻出来。\n\n不是比喻。D-████ 在班次末尾留下此便条后失联。接手键座的 D-████（替补）报告称，排字时偶尔看见铅字在字盘格外移动——移向平时空着的那几格。\n\n她说那些格子本来就该有字。\n\n替补随后亦失联。键座已移交登记，版级存疑，待 ████████ 后重新评级。\n\n——F-044 代填记录已归档。工位现空置。",
      "text_en": "[Recovered Item RC-2291 · Found in Layer V Compositing Hall, D-████ station · Handwritten note, folded inside key lectern seam]\n\nThe letters come out through the gaps.\n\nNot a figure of speech. D-████ left this note at shift's end and was subsequently reported missing. The replacement assigned to the lectern (D-████) reported observing leaden glyphs moving outside their designated trays — toward positions that had always been left unoccupied.\n\nShe said those positions were always supposed to have something in them.\n\nThe replacement was also later reported missing. The lectern has been logged for reassignment. Gradus pending ████████ re-evaluation.\n\n— F-044 proxy filing complete. Station currently unoccupied."
    }
