    "doc": {
      "text_zh": "回收物 RC-2271 · 发现于第 III 层铸字坊更衣格 · 布质护腕（左手，单只）\n\n织物材质：粗棉衬以铜丝。腕部内侧绣有细密的文字，肉眼不可辨。经显微镜阅读，全文为单句无限重复：",
      "text_en": "Recovered Item RC-2271 · Found in Layer III Casting Hall · Cloth wrist guard (left, single)\n\nMaterial: coarse cotton reinforced with copper thread. Inner surface bears dense embroidery, illegible to the naked eye. Magnified: a single phrase repeating without terminus — \"The key descends. The key has not yet descended.\" No seam indicates where the inscription begins or ends.\n\nLast assigned to: D-3847. Reported to intake that the wrist guard \"keeps slipping backward\" — that is, toward the elbow rather than the hand. No mechanical defect was found.\n\nSubsequent observations during containment inscription sessions: D-3847 completed each sequence fractionally before the preceding sequence concluded. Differential was consistent. Cause not determined.\n\nD-3847 later reported hearing \"something dripping\" during sessions. No moisture source identified in the vicinity.\n\nStatus: D-3847 transferred per §4.2. Item retained for further observation. Dripping sound continues to be logged at irregular intervals. No liquid present."
    }
