    "doc": {
      "text_zh": "物件档案 · 编号 SA-2291\n收录编号：SA-2291 · 版级：脱版 / Solum · 发现层：第 VIII 层\n物件描述：七色金属丝绕制的小球，各色丝线来源不明，熔点各异，理应无法相互缠绕而不断裂。现存完好。\n观察记录：D-4872、D-4873 在第 VIII 层协同作业期间领取此物，共用一枚，分属不同铭文组编制。值班守卷人注意到两人在铭刻期间",
      "text_en": "Object Log · SA-2291 · Gradus Formae: Solum\nRecovery Layer: VIII · Physical Form: A small sphere wound from seven distinct metal wires. Origins of each wire unverified. Melting points are mutually incompatible. The sphere has not come apart.\nObservation: D-4872 and D-4873 were assigned to SA-2291 during concurrent operations on Layer VIII, each attached to a separate inscription. The attending Lector noted that during inscription sessions, both subjects' hands moved 'as though answering each other.' Neither subject reported awareness of the other's actions. Upon separation of the two, D-4872 described the sensation of 'half of something' remaining in her palm. SA-2291 was recovered from the junction between their two workstations. Its position had not been moved. D-4873's station was ████ at time of collection.\nRemark: Reassigned to single-subject intake per §3.7. Anomalous weight reports persist."
    }
