    "doc": {
      "text_zh": "圣器登记档案 · SA-0774\n物品名称：贤者之石（Lapis Sapientis）\n外观：一枚磨光炉甘石，拇指大，绕以黄铜丝。表面蜡封处可见微小压印，经辨认为铸字坊旧日货币戳记。\n版级：熔版 / Fusum\n发现地点：第 IV 层铸字坊北侧坩埚旁，搁置于一只未盛任何物的铅水勺内。\n\n观察记录：\n接触该物后，D-2291 被分配至第 III 层普通铭刻值班。首日无异常。第三日，D-2291 提交 F-017 事件报告，称铭刻时",
      "text_en": "Sacred Artifact Registry · SA-0774\nItem: Lapis Sapientis (Sage's Stone)\nAppearance: A polished piece of calamine, thumb-sized, wound with brass wire. Wax seal on the surface bears a faint stamp — identified as a defunct coinage mark from the Casting Foundry.\nGradus Formae: Fusum\nRecovery Site: Layer IV, north furnace bay; found resting inside an empty lead-ladle.\n\nObservation Log:\nFollowing contact, D-2291 was assigned standard inscription duty on Layer III. Day one: unremarkable. Day three: D-2291 submitted Form F-017 stating that during inscription, the keys felt — \n[remainder of report continues in form F-017-2291-C, access level: ██]\n\nAttached note, handwritten, undated:"
    }
