    "doc": {
      "text_zh": "圣器档案 SA-2291\n版级：脱版 / Solum\n物品描述：一只折边磨损的帆布收集袋，印有第 V 层铅屑回收站标记。袋口缝有铜丝绳，无论开合多少次，结始终以同一角度收紧。\n\n发现经过：D-3847 在完成铭文组移交后，被观察到反复打开并检视该袋内壁。其描述袋内",
      "text_en": "Sacred Artifact Archive SA-2291\nGrading: Solum\nItem: A worn canvas collection satchel, stamped with the Level V lead-shavings recovery depot mark. Copper-wire drawstring closes to the same angle regardless of how many times it is opened.\n\nNotes: D-3847 was observed repeatedly opening and examining the bag's interior following each Inscription relinquishment. Subject reported the bag felt 'heavier after each return, never lighter.' Weight measurements taken over eleven sessions showed no deviation from baseline.\n\nAttached Phenomenon: Surplus plumbum tallies filed by D-3847 increased by a consistent margin across all recorded sessions. No surplus material was physically recovered from the satchel. D-3847 was asked to account for the discrepancy. Transcript of response: '████████████████████.'\n\nDisposition: Satchel transferred to Level V depot pending reclassification. Depot supervisor submitted F-017 noting the satchel 'was already there when we arrived.' Cross-reference: SA-2291-A. Access: ██-clearance."
    }
