      "text_en": "Incident Report IR-2██\nDate: M.2██.██.██\nItem: SA-0██(provisional designation: \"The Tilted Flask\")\nVersion: Mobilum\nDiscovery site: Layer IV, Pressroom Sub-corridor C\n\nDescription: A brass oil flask, dented on one side, with a hairline crack along the base. The interior contains residue consistent with standard press-lubrication oil. The flask cannot be filled past two-thirds capacity; attempts to do so result in the excess immediately evaporating. Origin of dent and crack: unrecorded.\n\nObservation: Keybound personnel carrying SA-0██ were monitored across ██ standard ascents. In intervals where the Hourglass Humour registered critically low, a consistent pattern emerged: witnesses reported hearing the crack along the flask's base emit a faint tone — described variously as \"a nail struck against copper,\" \"a bell with no body,\" and \"the sound a word makes before you say it.\" In the same intervals, Fracture frequency among holders showed statistically improbable elevation. Causal relationship: not established.\n\nD-3██ (holder, ascent 7) stated during post-ascent questioning: \"It gets louder when I'm almost out of time. I don't know how I know that. I just hit harder.\"\n\nD-3██ was reported missing on ascent 8. The flask was recovered at Layer IV checkpoint. The crack along the base had widened by approximately 1.2mm. No other changes noted.\n\nNote: Replacement holder D-3██ reports no auditory phenomena. Fracture anomaly persists regardless. Recommend continued monitoring under §4.2 standard loss-rotation protocol. F-017 filed. No further action required."
