    "doc": {
      "text_zh": "圣器收容记录 · 编号 SA-2241\n版级：脱版 / Solum\n\n物件描述：一段焊接于排字棒后端的铜质线圈，接头已氧化，绕线方向与标准规格相反。回收自第 VII 层机械外壳东侧配电夹层，与 ████ 同批移交。\n\n观测记录：凡持有 SA-2241 的键徒，其周遭工位的铭文组在其铭刻时会发出同频颤鸣，但不见操作者触碰。最早由 D-2901 的同僚察觉——据报，D-2901 铭刻时邻位的 D-2903 手指同步抽动，后者本人否认有所察觉，亦无相关记忆。\n\n附带记录：D-2901 于 M.2██.03.██ 失联。D-2903 申请换班。申请已归档。换班未执行。\n\n备注：SA-2241 绕线方向问题已提交工程存档 EG-████，回复意见为",
      "text_en": "Sacred Artifact Record · SA-2241\nGradus Formae: Solum\n\nDescription: A copper coil welded to the rear of a composing stick, oxidised at both terminals, wound in the direction opposite to standard specification. Recovered from the electrical interstitial of Layer VII's eastern mechanical shell, transferred alongside ████.\n\nObservations: Keybound personnel in possession of SA-2241 report that adjacent lectern positions emit harmonic tremors during their inscription strokes — without contact. First noted by colleagues of D-2901: D-2903's fingers were observed moving in synchrony during D-2901's inscription session. D-2903 denied awareness. No corresponding memory reported.\n\nSupplementary: D-2901 was reported absent M.2██.03.██. D-2903 submitted a shift-change request. Request archived. Transfer not executed.\n\nNote: The irregular winding direction of SA-2241 was referred to engineering log EG-████. Response classified ██-grade. No further annotation recorded."
    }
